From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Piotr Kubaj <pkubaj@anongoth.pl>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 07:12:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 10047: Add FreeBSD PowerPC 64-bit platforms (freebsd_ppc_64,
 freebsd_ppc_64le)

FreeBSD runs on 64-bit PowerPC in both byte orders (uname -p powerpc64
and powerpc64le; the JVM reports os.arch "ppc64" and "ppc64le"). Ghidra
has no Platform for either, so Platform.CURRENT_PLATFORM is UNSUPPORTED
with a null directory name and the native decompiler, sleigh, demangler
and lzfse helpers are never found. The gradle native build refuses to
run there as well ("Unrecognized platform architecture: ppc64le").

Register the two platforms the same way freebsd_arm_64 is registered:

- Architecture: add POWERPC_64LE for os.arch "ppc64le" (POWERPC_64
  already matches the big-endian "ppc64").
- Platform: add FREEBSD_PPC_64 and FREEBSD_PPC_64LE with the os/
  directory names freebsd_ppc_64 and freebsd_ppc_64le. The two byte
  orders need separate directories because their native binaries are
  not interchangeable.
- nativePlatforms.gradle: add both to PLATFORMS and map the JVM
  architecture names to them in getCurrentPlatformName().
- Add both as targetPlatform of decompile, sleigh, lzfse and the two GNU
  demanglers.
- GettingStarted.md: list them with the other user-built platforms.

Like the other FreeBSD platforms there is no debugger support.

Tested on FreeBSD 15.1 powerpc64le and powerpc64 (POWER9) with the
12.0.4 release: the natives build with gradle 9.8, OpenJDK 25 and clang
19 (this is how the FreeBSD port devel/ghidra builds them), and with
Platform/Architecture rebuilt into Generic.jar a headless analysis of a
native ELF binary decompiles its functions through the new
os/freebsd_ppc_64le and os/freebsd_ppc_64 binaries, the GNU demangler
analyzer runs through the new demangler_gnu_v2_41, and sleigh compiles
a processor spec. lzfse builds on both, but as on any big-endian host
the Apple code reads and writes its stream headers in host byte order,
so only the little-endian binary produces and reads valid LZFSE data.
---
 GPL/nativePlatforms.gradle                     | 5 +++++
 Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/buildNatives.gradle | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/GPL/nativePlatforms.gradle b/GPL/nativePlatforms.gradle
index c0dbfe9568..0e282cc3d4 100644
--- a/GPL/nativePlatforms.gradle
+++ b/GPL/nativePlatforms.gradle
@@ -94,6 +94,11 @@ ext.getCurrentPlatformName = {
 		case "loongarch64":
 		case "loong64":
 			arch = "loongarch_64"
+		case "ppc64":
+			arch = "ppc_64"
+			break
+		case "ppc64le":
+			arch = "ppc_64le"
 			break
 		default:
 			throw new GradleException("Unrecognized platform architecture: $arch" )
diff --git a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/buildNatives.gradle b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/buildNatives.gradle
index 0ca38b14c2..d0abeaccc0 100644
--- a/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/buildNatives.gradle
+++ b/Ghidra/Features/Decompiler/buildNatives.gradle
@@ -362,6 +362,8 @@ model {
 				targetPlatform "mac_arm_64"
 				targetPlatform "freebsd_x86_64"
 				targetPlatform "freebsd_arm_64"
+				targetPlatform "freebsd_ppc_64"
+				targetPlatform "freebsd_ppc_64le"
 				targetPlatform "openbsd_x86_64"
 				targetPlatform "openbsd_arm_64"
 				sources {
@@ -413,6 +415,8 @@ model {
 				targetPlatform "mac_arm_64"
 				targetPlatform "freebsd_x86_64"
 				targetPlatform "freebsd_arm_64"
+				targetPlatform "freebsd_ppc_64"
+				targetPlatform "freebsd_ppc_64le"
 				targetPlatform "openbsd_x86_64"
 				targetPlatform "openbsd_arm_64"
 				sources {
